==============================================================================
S1  Three-row automaton: row of the j-th child, base row from u mod 18, rotation 1->5->3, tree to depth 6
==============================================================================
PROVED: for odd n, row(n) := n mod 6 = rho(3n+1 mod 9) with rho(4)=1, rho(1)=3, rho(7)=5.
   Proof: n = 6i+r gives 3n+1 = 18i + (3r+1), and 3r+1 = 4, 10=1, 16=7 mod 9 for r = 1, 3, 5.
   Same law in the F-convention of the row_braid lane: F(n)=(3n+1)/2 = 2^h u, row = rho_F(2^h u mod 9),
   rho_F(2)=1, rho_F(5)=3, rho_F(8)=5 (multiply by 2^{-1} = 5 mod 9: 4->2, 1->5, 7->8).
PROVED: row(n_j) = rho(2^(h0+1+2j) u mod 9); since 4 -> 16=7 -> 28=1 -> 4 (mod 9), j -> j+1 rotates the row
   1 -> 5 -> 3 -> 1 (i.e. +4 mod 6), exact period 3 = ord_9(4); every third child is a row-3 leaf.
   base row (j=0) from u mod 18:
   u mod 18 | u mod 9 | h0 | 2^(h0+1) u mod 9 | base row | rows of j=0..5
   1        | 1       | 1  | 4                | 1        | [1, 5, 3, 1, 5, 3]
   5        | 5       | 0  | 1                | 3        | [3, 1, 5, 3, 1, 5]
   7        | 7       | 1  | 1                | 3        | [3, 1, 5, 3, 1, 5]
   11       | 2       | 0  | 4                | 1        | [1, 5, 3, 1, 5, 3]
   13       | 4       | 1  | 7                | 5        | [5, 3, 1, 5, 3, 1]
   17       | 8       | 0  | 7                | 5        | [5, 3, 1, 5, 3, 1]
PROVED: base row = 1 for u = 1, 11 mod 18; 5 for u = 13, 17 mod 18; 3 (leaf) for u = 5, 7 mod 18;
   equivalently u mod 9 in {1,2} -> row 1, {4,8} -> row 5, {5,7} -> row 3.  Agrees with the row_braid table
   (its 'row' column for u mod 18 = 1,5,7,11,13,17 reads 1,3,3,1,5,5).
FINITE-EXACT: tree generated to depth 6 with j<=8: nodes per level [1, 8, 45, 270, 1620, 9720, 58320] (total 69984), 0.2s
   row counts per level (1: internal, 5: internal, 3: leaf): [{1: 2, 3: 3, 5: 3}, {1: 15, 3: 15, 5: 15}, {1: 90, 3: 90, 5: 90}, {1: 540, 3: 540, 5: 540}, {1: 3240, 3: 3240, 5: 3240}, {1: 19440, 3: 19440, 5: 19440}]
   every node satisfies T(n)=parent, row(n) = rho(2^(h0+1+2j) u mod 9) = base(u mod 18) + 4j mod 6;
   the only repeated node is the loop child(1,0) = 1 (1 repeat(s)); all other nodes distinct (T is a function).
   depth-D row pattern of the descendant along an index path (j_1,...,j_D):
   D=1 path=(0,): function of u mod 9 (checked all odd u < 54), NOT of u mod 3 (witness class 1 mod 3)
   D=2 path=(0, 0): function of u mod 27 (checked all odd u < 162), NOT of u mod 9 (witness class 1 mod 9)
   D=3 path=(0, 0, 0): function of u mod 81 (checked all odd u < 486), NOT of u mod 27 (witness class 1 mod 27)
   D=4 path=(0, 0, 0, 0): function of u mod 243 (checked all odd u < 1458), NOT of u mod 81 (witness class 1 mod 81)
PROVED: along a fixed index path the rows of the first D descendants depend only on u mod 3^(D+1)
   (n_j = (2^a u - 1)/3 sends u mod 3^(s+1) to n_j mod 3^s, and the row of an odd node is its residue mod 3:
   1 -> row 1, 0 -> row 3, 2 -> row 5, checked for odd n < 20001; induct on D),
   and FINITE-EXACT sharp for D<=4 (some class mod 3^D splits; a class whose path reaches a leaf cannot split).
   This is the tree-side twin of the E-graph lane's Theorem 4.1 (greedy letters k_1..k_J are a function of
   m mod 3^(J+1), sharp).

